1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
 Your birth date holds two numbers, and

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,120
 most people calculate at least one of

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:05,000
 them wrong.

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,310
 Maybe you looked yours up once and got an

5
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:10,230
 11. Then another site gave you a 2 and

6
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:12,000
 you stopped trusting any of it.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,510
 In the next few minutes you'll learn both

8
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:16,180
 numbers, the 9 planets behind them and

9
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,000
 the grid hidden inside your date.

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,240
 Then you'll work out your own in 30

11
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,000
 seconds.

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,190
 In Vedic numerology, the first number is

13
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:29,320
 your Moolank. Moolank means root

14
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,000
 number.

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,150
 It comes only from the day of the month

16
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:34,000
 you were born, nothing else.

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,440
 Take one example. Someone born on the 14th

18
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,000
 of August, 1996.

19
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
 The day is 14. Add its digits. 1 + 4 is 5.

20
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
 Moolank 5.

21
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,120
 If you were born on a single digit day,

22
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:49,170
 like the 7th, that digit is already your

23
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:50,000
 Moolank.

24
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
 If you were born on the 29th, 2 + 9 is 11.

25
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,200
 11 still has two digits, so keep going. 1

26
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,000
 + 1 is 2. Moolank 2.

27
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,150
 Your Moolank is how you move through an

28
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:04,350
 ordinary day. It's the version of you

29
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:06,000
 that people meet first.

30
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,760
 The second number is your Bhagyank. Bhagyank

31
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:15,000
 means the number of fortune.

32
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,520
 This one uses the whole date. Day, month

33
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:20,000
 and year. Every single digit.

34
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,990
 For the 14th of August, 1996, that's 1, 4,

35
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:28,000
 0, 8, 1, 9, 9, 6.

36
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,770
 Add them together and you get 38. 3 + 8

37
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:35,000
 is 11. 1 + 1 is 2. Bhagyank 2.

38
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,760
 So your Moolank is how you act. Your Bhagyank

39
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,590
 is the direction your life keeps pulling

40
00:01:39,590 --> 00:01:42,000
 you, whether you planned it or not.

41
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,340
 Every number from 1 to 9 belongs to a

42
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:51,000
 planet. Here they are, one line each.

43
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,060
 1 is the Sun. Leading and standing on

44
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,000
 your own.

45
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,760
 2 is the Moon. Feeling, partnership and

46
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,000
 quiet care.

47
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,020
 3 is Jupiter. Wisdom, teaching and clear

48
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:05,000
 values.

49
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,040
 4 is Rahu. A sharp, restless mind that

50
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:10,000
 does things its own way.

51
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,950
 5 is Mercury. Quick thinking, talking and

52
00:02:13,950 --> 00:02:15,000
 trading.

53
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,820
 6 is Venus. Love, beauty and looking

54
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:20,000
 after the people around you.

55
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,040
 7 is Ketu. Depth, intuition and looking

56
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:26,000
 under the surface.

57
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,690
 8 is Saturn. Hard work, patience and

58
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,000
 results that come late but stay.

59
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,330
 9 is Mars. Courage, energy and standing

60
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,000
 up for what's right.

61
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,960
 So our example has Moolank 5, Mercury

62
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:43,000
 and Bhagyank 2, the Moon.

63
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,130
 Most people have two different numbers,

64
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:51,000
 and you can feel the gap between them.

65
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,880
 Our example moves like Mercury. Fast,

66
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:57,000
 talking, always working something out.

67
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,850
 But life keeps steering them toward the

68
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:00,930
 moon. Toward people, toward feelings,

69
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:03,000
 toward being the one everyone leans on.

70
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,220
 It can feel like being two people. The

71
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,490
 one who gets through a busy Tuesday, and

72
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:10,000
 the one your life keeps asking you to be.

73
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,320
 Neither one is a mistake. The work is

74
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:15,000
 knowing which one is in charge right now.

75
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,350
 If your two numbers are the same, there's

76
00:03:17,350 --> 00:03:19,270
 no gap. That one planet just shows up

77
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:20,000
 twice as strong.

78
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
 In the easy parts, and in the hard ones.

79
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,200
 Now the part most people never see. The

80
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,000
 Vedic grid.

81
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,310
 It's a 3x3 box, and each of the nine

82
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:35,000
 numbers has its own seat.

83
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,000
 Top row, 3, 1, 9. Middle row, 6, 7, 5.

84
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
 Bottom row, 2, 8, 4.

85
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,520
 To fill it, take the digits of your birth

86
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,610
 date, but use only the last two digits of

87
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:52,000
 the year, and skip every zero.

88
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,750
 Then add your Bhagyank. And if you were

89
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:57,000
 born on a two-digit day, like the 14th,

90
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
 add your Moolank too.

91
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
 The 10th, 20th, and 30th don't count.

92
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:07,000
 For our example, that's 1, 4, 8, 9, and 6.

93
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,330
 Then Moolank 5, and Bhagyank 2. Each

94
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:12,000
 digit takes its seat.

95
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,350
 Now look at what's empty. 3 and 7. Those

96
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:17,000
 are the missing numbers.

97
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,530
 A missing number is a planet with no

98
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:21,000
 place in your grid.

99
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,650
 Here, Jupiter and Ketu. It doesn't mean

100
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:25,000
 something is wrong with you.

101
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
 It means that quality isn't handed to you.

102
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,530
 You build it on purpose, usually later,

103
00:04:30,530 --> 00:04:32,000
 and often the hard way.

104
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,270
 And a number that shows up twice gets

105
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:35,000
 louder.

106
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,020
 Someone born on the 29th of March, 1990,

107
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,460
 has two 2s and two 9s in their grid, and

108
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:43,000
 five empty seats.

109
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
 So why do so many people get this wrong?

110
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
 Three mistakes.

111
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,530
 Mistake 1, keeping master numbers.

112
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:56,950
 Western numerology stops at 11, 22, or 33,

113
00:04:56,950 --> 00:04:59,000
 and calls them master numbers.

114
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,530
 Vedic numerology always goes down to one

115
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:04,070
 digit, because there are nine planets,

116
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:05,000
 not 33.

117
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,380
 Our example's 38 becomes 11, and a

118
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:09,000
 Western site stops there.

119
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
 Here, 11 becomes 2, the Moon.

120
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
 The 29th of March, 1990, adds up to 33.

121
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,100
 Western says master 33. Vedic says 6,

122
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,000
 Venus.

123
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
 Mistake 2, the wrong grid.

124
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,520
 Many apps use a different layout, with 4,

125
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,000
 9, 2 along the top.

126
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,520
 Same nine numbers, different seats, so

127
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:33,000
 every pattern you read from it shifts.

128
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
 The Vedic grid starts 3, 1, 9.

129
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,420
 Mistake 3, putting the whole year in the

130
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,000
 grid.

131
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,820
 The 19 or the 20 belongs in your Bhagyank,

132
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:44,000
 not in your grid.

133
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,750
 Put it in the grid, and you get a 1, a 9,

134
00:05:46,750 --> 00:05:49,000
 or a 2 that isn't really yours.

135
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
 Here's yours, in 30 seconds.

136
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
 Pause if you need to.

137
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,080
 1. Take your birth day and add its digits

138
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,000
 until one digit is left.

139
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
 That's your Moolank.

140
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,680
 2. Add every digit of your full date, and

141
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:07,000
 keep going until one digit is left.

142
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,990
 Don't stop at 11, 22, or 33. That's your

143
00:06:10,990 --> 00:06:12,000
 Bhagyank.

144
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
 3. Find both planets on the list.

145
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,230
 4. Draw the grid and see which seats stay

146
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:19,000
 empty.

147
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
 Or skip the arithmetic.

148
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
 Go to numevix.com/try.

149
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,150
 Type your date, and the free calculator

150
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:28,000
 does all of it, grid included.

151
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,550
 Then comment your birth date below, day,

152
00:06:30,550 --> 00:06:34,000
 month, year, and the two numbers you got.

153
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,270
 Let's see how many of you were handed an

154
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,000
 11.

155
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,120
 And if you want your whole year ahead,

156
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,000
 read through your numbers.

157
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
 The annual forecast is on the site.

